{"case_id":"T8023","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry point","API protocol","input semantics","attack surface"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["parseAndPrintFile","xmllintShell","xmllintMain"],"reason":"S1 makes the interactive shell path reachable in fuzz builds by removing the XMLLINT_FUZZ guard around `if (lint->shell)`, but H0 neither supplies `--shell` nor fuzzes the shell command stream consumed by `xmllintShell`. Consequently, document-dependent shell operations and their interactive input protocol are not exercised.","evidence":["In S1, `parseAndPrintFile` unconditionally checks `lint->shell` and calls `xmllintShell(doc, filename, stdout)`; the surrounding `#ifndef XMLLINT_FUZZ` and `#endif` were removed.","H0's `switches[]` contains no `--shell`, so its generated argv cannot select `lint->shell`.","H0 partitions fuzz data into option values, strings, entities, and `docBuffer`/`docUrl`, then calls `xmllintMain`; it does not route fuzz bytes to the stdin command protocol used by the interactive shell.","S1 declares `xmllintShell(xmlDocPtr doc, const char *filename, FILE *output)` alongside the newly exposed `xmllintMain` in `private/lint.h`, confirming the shell is a distinct document-processing interface reached from `parseAndPrintFile`."],"recommended_action":"Add dedicated shell coverage that parses a fuzzed document, enables `--shell`, and provides a bounded fuzz-derived stdin command stream to `xmllintShell`; alternatively invoke `xmllintShell` directly with controlled input/output plumbing and reset global/parser state between iterations."}
